# Line endings, so a checkout on Windows builds the same as one on macOS.
#
# Git's own heuristic already treats a keystore as binary — it holds NUL bytes well inside the
# block Git inspects — but the heuristic is not the only thing in play. A developer with
# `* text=auto eol=crlf` in a global config, or a tool that rewrites the working tree, turns the
# lone LF bytes inside `example/android/app/debug.keystore` into CRLF and the file grows. Gradle
# then fails with `Invalid keystore format` on that machine only, from a file the diff says nobody
# touched. Naming it here removes the dependency on per-developer config.
#
# The Gradle wrapper needs no entry: `gradlew`, `gradlew.bat` and `gradle-wrapper.jar` are not
# tracked in this repository — the Flutter tool writes them on first build. See
# example/android/.gitignore.
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.p12 binary
